# Dev-only: point the BFF's Firebase Admin SDK at the emulator suite.
#
# Why this file has to exist. The Firebase CLI injects both of these into the
# FUNCTIONS runtime, but the BFF is started by Bun (`bun run bff:dev`), so it
# inherits neither. Without them, in dev, while the browser IS on the emulator:
#
#   * FIREBASE_AUTH_EMULATOR_HOST — every token fails verification. Emulator ID
#     tokens are unsigned (header `{"alg":"none","typ":"JWT"}`, empty signature,
#     no `kid`; see the note in `bff/security.ts`), and firebase-admin only
#     accepts those when it knows it is talking to an emulator. The symptom is
#     `/event` logging "Firebase ID token has no kid claim" on every heartbeat,
#     and — much worse — `isJwtAuth` answering `401 invalid_token` on EVERY
#     authenticated `/api` route, so `/api/orgs`, billing and machines all fail
#     for a signed-in user.
#
#   * FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST — with this unset the BFF talks to the LIVE
#     `easyscrape` database (`dbName` resolves to `easyscrape` from
#     `env.DB_NAME`) while the browser reads the emulator. Dev testing would
#     then read and write real user and billing documents.
#
# Loaded ONLY by `bun run bff:dev` via `bun --env-file`. No deploy script
# references it, and `bff/security.ts` still refuses to boot when
# FIREBASE_AUTH_EMULATOR_HOST is set together with `PRODUCTION=true`, so this
# cannot make a deployed BFF trust unsigned tokens.
FIREBASE_AUTH_EMULATOR_HOST=127.0.0.1:9099
FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST=127.0.0.1:5001

# The scraping engine. `WEBRAIN_MCP_URL` has NO default on purpose
# (`config/env.ts`), so an unconfigured process reports every webrain-backed
# route as `transportError` -> 502 "The scraping worker is unreachable", which
# is what `/api/search` and `/api/crawl` do (SCRAPE_PROVIDER defaults to
# webrain). Point it at the local worker:
#
#   D:\Windows\Documents\Programming\Projects\Rust\webrain\target\debug\webrain.exe mcp --http 9333
#
# A loopback bind needs no token, so nothing secret belongs in this file — it is
# TRACKED (see the `!bff/.env.dev` rule in .gitignore). To use the deployed
# engine instead, change this to https://mcp.deepscrape.dev and pass
# WEBRAIN_HTTP_TOKEN in the shell for that process; never commit it here.
WEBRAIN_MCP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9333
